<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · British Isles</p><h1 class="st-title">The Protectorate</h1><p class="st-meta">1653 CE – 1659 CE · capital London</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The phase of the English republic in which Oliver Cromwell, and briefly his son Richard, ruled as Lord Protector of England, Scotland and Ireland.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In December 1653, after the failure of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/barebones-parliament">Barebone's Parliament</a>, army officers drew up the Instrument of Government, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain's</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/1931-constitution-of-ethiopia">first written constitution</a>, which made <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oliver-cromwell">Oliver Cromwell</a> Lord Protector of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/commonwealth-of-england">Commonwealth of England, Scotland and Ireland</a>, with a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/english-council-of-state">Council of State</a> and Parliament.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oliver-cromwell">Cromwell</a> governed with mixed success: he quarrelled with his Parliaments, divided the country under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rule-of-the-major-generals">Major-Generals</a> in 1655 to 1657 and refused the crown in 1657, accepting instead the Humble Petition and Advice. Abroad, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">Protectorate</a> made peace with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a>, fought <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> and seized <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/jamaica">Jamaica</a> in 1655. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jews">Jews</a> were informally allowed to resettle in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> from 1656.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oliver-cromwell">Oliver</a> died in September 1658 and was succeeded by his son Richard, who lacked army support and resigned in May 1659. The <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/commonwealth-of-england">Commonwealth of England</a> was restored briefly before the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stuart-restoration">Restoration of 1660</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/the-protectorate.jpg" alt="The Protectorate" width="320" height="256"><figcaption>Image: Richtom80 at English Wikipedia · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_The_Commonwealth.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1653 CE – 1659 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>London</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Oliver Cromwell, Richard Cromwell</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Protestant Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>English</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/united-kingdom">United Kingdom</a>, <a href="/countries/ireland">Ireland</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Protectorate of Oliver Cromwell</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1656&amp;focus=the-protectorate" aria-label="The Protectorate on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4677 395 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where The Protectorate lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M4997 651L4997 651"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M4997 651h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4997 651h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M4997 651h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks London. <a href="/atlas?year=1656&amp;focus=the-protectorate">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
